# Regression: `HashSet[P] s = {}` (empty literal) — HashSet struct-payload
# cell of the Round XXIV Track E axis matrix (Set/HashSet share the arm, so
# HashSet coverage keeps the axis matrix honest against a partial regression).
# Pre-fix: same C-emit "incompatible types when assigning to type 'GorgetSet'
# from type 'int32_t'" as the Set__ cells because `infer_collection_element_type`
# had no `HashSet__` arm either.
#
# HashSet REQUIRES `@derive(Equatable, Hashable)` on the payload
# (`E_UnsatisfiedTraitBound` otherwise). HashSet iteration order is unordered
# (hash-table), so only membership / count is asserted — a `for` sum keeps it
# deterministic.
@derive(Equatable, Hashable)
struct P:
    int x
    int y
    int z

int main():
    HashSet[P] s = {}
    s.add(P(1, 2, 3))
    s.add(P(4, 5, 6))
    print(s.len())
    int total = 0
    for p in s:
        total = total + p.x + p.y + p.z
    print(f"{total}")
    return 0
